    Examples
    --------
    >>> a = ma.arange(24).reshape(2,3,4)
    >>> a[:,0,1] = ma.masked
    >>> a[:,1,:] = ma.masked
    >>> print(a)
    [[[0 -- 2 3]
      [-- -- -- --]
      [8 9 10 11]]

     [[12 -- 14 15]
      [-- -- -- --]
      [20 21 22 23]]]
    >>> print(ma.apply_over_axes(ma.sum, a, [0,2]))
    [[[46]
      [--]
      [124]]]

    Tuple axis arguments to ufuncs are equivalent:

    >>> print(ma.sum(a, axis=(0,2)).reshape((1,-1,1)))
    [[[46]
      [--]
      [124]]]
