        Return the imaginary part of the masked array.

        The returned array is a view on the imaginary part of the `MaskedArray`
        whose `get_imag` method is called.

        Parameters
        ----------
        None

        Returns
        -------
        result : MaskedArray
            The imaginary part of the masked array.

        See Also
        --------
        get_real, real, imag

        Examples
        --------
        >>> x = np.ma.array([1+1.j, -2j, 3.45+1.6j], mask=[False, True, False])
        >>> x.get_imag()
        masked_array(data = [1.0 -- 1.6],
                     mask = [False  True False],
               fill_value = 1e+20)

        )r4␀␀Úimagr6␀␀r,␀␀r¥␀␀r:␀␀)r=␀␀r'␀␀rË␀␀␀rË␀␀␀rÌ␀␀␀Úget_imagã␀␀s␀␀␀␀zMaskedArray.get_imagzImaginary part.c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀C␀␀␀s"␀␀␀|␀j␀jjt|␀ƒƒ}|j|␀jƒ␀|S␀)aŸ␀␀
        Return the real part of the masked array.

        The returned array is a view on the real part of the `MaskedArray`
        whose `get_real` method is called.

        Parameters
        ----------
        None

        Returns
        -------
        result : MaskedArray
            The real part of the masked array.

        See Also
        --------
        get_imag, real, imag

        Examples
        --------
        >>> x = np.ma.array([1+1.j, -2j, 3.45+1.6j], mask=[False, True, False])
        >>> x.get_real()
        masked_array(data = [1.0 -- 3.45],
                     mask = [False  True False],
               fill_value = 1e+20)

