„␀ZdS␀)r␀␀␀aŞ␀␀ Represents a single parameter to a test case.

        For example::

            >>> p = param("foo", bar=16)
            >>> p
            param("foo", bar=16)
            >>> p.args
            ('foo', )
            >>> p.kwargs
            {'bar': 16}

        Intended to be used as an argument to ``@parameterized``::

            @parameterized([
                param("foo", bar=16),
            ])
            def test_stuff(foo, bar=16):
                pass
        c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀O␀␀␀s␀␀␀t␀j|␀||ƒS␀)N)Ú_paramÚ__new__)ÚclsÚargsÚkwargsr␀␀␀r␀␀␀r␀␀␀r␀␀␀a␀␀␀s␀␀␀␀zparam.__new__Nc␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀C␀␀␀s␀␀␀|pf␀}|pi␀}|␀||S␀)a␀␀ Creates a ``param`` by explicitly specifying ``args`` and
