    Return the shape of an array.

    Parameters
    ----------
    a : array_like
        Input array.

    Returns
    -------
    shape : tuple of ints
        The elements of the shape tuple give the lengths of the
        corresponding array dimensions.

    See Also
    --------
    alen
    ndarray.shape : Equivalent array method.

    Examples
    --------
    >>> np.shape(np.eye(3))
    (3, 3)
    >>> np.shape([[1, 2]])
    (1, 2)
    >>> np.shape([0])
    (1,)
    >>> np.shape(0)
    ()

    >>> a = np.array([(1, 2), (3, 4)], dtype=[('x', 'i4'), ('y', 'i4')])
    >>> np.shape(a)
    (2,)
    >>> a.shape
    (2,)

